1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,240
What's today's video about? It's about Japanese summer foods!

2
00:00:09,240 --> 00:00:10,740
Scene 1: The Fun of Nagashi Somen / How to Enjoy Flowing Noodles

3
00:00:10,740 --> 00:00:14,974
This place is in the mountains, isn't it?

4
00:00:14,997 --> 00:00:18,091
It's so refreshing here!

5
00:00:18,114 --> 00:00:21,548
The river water is so clear.

6
00:00:21,571 --> 00:00:26,248
Look, there's bamboo!

7
00:00:26,271 --> 00:00:30,238
This is nagashi somen—flowing noodles!

8
00:00:30,261 --> 00:00:32,927
That looks fun!

9
00:00:32,950 --> 00:00:36,350
Let's grab our chopsticks and wait.

10
00:00:36,373 --> 00:00:39,445
Oh, here comes the somen!

11
00:00:39,469 --> 00:00:43,127
Wow, it's really fast!

12
00:00:43,151 --> 00:00:47,219
Oh no, it's gone!

13
00:00:47,243 --> 00:00:51,055
It's so hard to catch!

14
00:00:51,079 --> 00:00:53,212
Wait for it...

15
00:00:53,235 --> 00:00:55,702
Here comes another one!

16
00:00:55,725 --> 00:00:58,691
Oh, the next one is here!

17
00:00:58,714 --> 00:01:00,785
Hurry, grab it!

18
00:01:00,809 --> 00:01:04,709
Oh no, it got away again!

19
00:01:04,732 --> 00:01:07,622
Stay focused!

20
00:01:07,645 --> 00:01:10,491
The water's flowing too fast!

21
00:01:10,515 --> 00:01:13,766
Let me try this time.

22
00:01:13,790 --> 00:01:15,926
Good luck!

23
00:01:15,949 --> 00:01:17,683
Here it comes!

24
00:01:17,706 --> 00:01:20,725
Got it!

25
00:01:20,748 --> 00:01:23,220
Nice!

26
00:01:23,244 --> 00:01:24,982
You're so good at this!

27
00:01:25,005 --> 00:01:28,544
Dip it in the sauce and eat it.

28
00:01:28,567 --> 00:01:30,967
It's so delicious!

29
00:01:30,990 --> 00:01:34,123
I want to try it too!

30
00:01:34,146 --> 00:01:37,113
Next time, I'll definitely catch it!

31
00:01:37,136 --> 00:01:39,269
Here it comes!

32
00:01:39,292 --> 00:01:41,580
It's coming from the right!

33
00:01:41,603 --> 00:01:44,570
Yes! I got it!

34
00:01:44,593 --> 00:01:46,926
You did it!

35
00:01:46,949 --> 00:01:49,194
Congratulations!

36
00:01:49,217 --> 00:01:51,584
I'm so happy!

37
00:01:51,607 --> 00:01:54,852
It's so cold and tasty!

38
00:01:54,875 --> 00:01:58,521
This is so fun—let's eat a lot!

39
00:01:58,545 --> 00:02:00,345
Sure!

40
00:02:00,368 --> 00:02:03,901
I wish more noodles would come!

41
00:02:03,924 --> 00:02:08,994
The staff is preparing more, so please wait a moment.

42
00:02:09,018 --> 00:02:11,109
Got it!

43
00:02:11,132 --> 00:02:14,332
I'll get my chopsticks ready.

44
00:02:14,355 --> 00:02:23,364
You can download today's video script from the description and top comment.

45
00:02:23,364 --> 00:02:24,864
Scene 2: How to Eat Hiyashi Chuka / Enjoying Cold Ramen

46
00:02:24,864 --> 00:02:27,997
It's so hot today, isn't it?

47
00:02:28,020 --> 00:02:30,053
Yeah, it really is.

48
00:02:30,076 --> 00:02:32,495
I'm getting hungry.

49
00:02:32,519 --> 00:02:36,530
I bought hiyashi chuka from the convenience store!

50
00:02:36,553 --> 00:02:39,003
Hiyashi chuka, huh?

51
00:02:39,026 --> 00:02:41,360
That looks delicious!

52
00:02:41,384 --> 00:02:44,022
Alright, let's dig in!

53
00:02:44,046 --> 00:02:45,446
Huh?

54
00:02:45,469 --> 00:02:49,402
Wow, there's a lot in the bag!

55
00:02:49,425 --> 00:02:52,992
Yeah, there's soup and toppings inside.

56
00:02:53,015 --> 00:02:55,711
Is this water?

57
00:02:55,734 --> 00:02:59,782
That's water to loosen the noodles.

58
00:02:59,805 --> 00:03:02,475
Do we rinse the noodles?

59
00:03:02,499 --> 00:03:05,910
No, we don't.

60
00:03:05,934 --> 00:03:08,341
We pour it over the noodles.

61
00:03:08,364 --> 00:03:10,901
Then mix it all together.

62
00:03:10,925 --> 00:03:12,725
I see.

63
00:03:12,748 --> 00:03:15,589
So we pour the water first, right?

64
00:03:15,613 --> 00:03:17,089
Sure!

65
00:03:17,112 --> 00:03:20,748
After that, add the soup.

66
00:03:20,771 --> 00:03:23,304
Soup added!

67
00:03:23,327 --> 00:03:26,094
What's next?

68
00:03:26,117 --> 00:03:29,334
Put the toppings on the noodles.

69
00:03:29,358 --> 00:03:32,891
Ham, egg, and cucumber, right?

70
00:03:32,914 --> 00:03:35,789
It looks so pretty!

71
00:03:35,812 --> 00:03:39,346
This is mustard and mayonnaise.

72
00:03:39,369 --> 00:03:42,615
Should we add mayonnaise too?

73
00:03:42,638 --> 00:03:45,205
Add it if you like!

74
00:03:45,227 --> 00:03:47,724
I'll add some.

75
00:03:47,748 --> 00:03:51,020
I'll just add mustard.

76
00:03:51,043 --> 00:03:54,686
There's a lot to do before eating, huh?

77
00:03:54,710 --> 00:03:57,127
For sure!

78
00:03:57,150 --> 00:04:01,165
It's like a little puzzle.

79
00:04:01,189 --> 00:04:04,648
But we're finally done!

80
00:04:04,671 --> 00:04:07,604
Now we can eat!

81
00:04:07,627 --> 00:04:09,227
Bon appétit!

82
00:04:09,250 --> 00:04:11,650
How does it taste?

83
00:04:11,673 --> 00:04:15,207
It's so tangy and delicious!

84
00:04:15,230 --> 00:04:17,996
So refreshing!

85
00:04:18,019 --> 00:04:21,186
Perfect for summer, right?

86
00:04:21,209 --> 00:04:22,542
Absolutely!

87
00:04:22,565 --> 00:04:25,299
I could eat this every day!

88
00:04:25,322 --> 00:04:29,090
Next time, let's try something from a different convenience store!

89
00:04:29,113 --> 00:04:30,805
Sounds good!

90
00:04:30,829 --> 00:04:33,795
Let's eat together again!

91
00:04:33,818 --> 00:04:40,923
You can review today's video with the link in the description and top comment! *Note: The site may be removed without notice.

92
00:04:40,923 --> 00:04:42,423
Scene 3: Summer Festival Shaved Ice Stalls

93
00:04:42,423 --> 00:04:46,096
The festival is so lively!

94
00:04:46,120 --> 00:04:50,725
Yeah, there are so many people!

95
00:04:50,748 --> 00:04:55,282
It's hot, so let's get some shaved ice!

96
00:04:55,304 --> 00:04:57,238
Sounds good!

97
00:04:57,261 --> 00:05:00,753
There's a stall over there!

98
00:05:00,776 --> 00:05:03,071
Check out the menu!

99
00:05:03,095 --> 00:05:06,702
There are so many flavors!

100
00:05:06,725 --> 00:05:10,960
Strawberry, melon, lemon...

101
00:05:10,984 --> 00:05:15,184
Oh, there's Blue Hawaii!

102
00:05:15,207 --> 00:05:19,854
Blue Hawaii? What does it taste like?

103
00:05:19,878 --> 00:05:23,116
Alright, let's guess the flavor.

104
00:05:23,139 --> 00:05:25,413
Go ahead, give it a try.

105
00:05:25,436 --> 00:05:27,806
Hmm, I can't tell.

106
00:05:27,829 --> 00:05:31,163
I'll go with Blue Hawaii.

107
00:05:31,187 --> 00:05:34,066
I'll have strawberry.

108
00:05:34,090 --> 00:05:37,762
Excuse me, I'll take these two, please.

109
00:05:37,785 --> 00:05:42,230
Wow, this blue shaved ice looks so pretty!

110
00:05:42,254 --> 00:05:46,094
Yeah, it's cold and delicious.

111
00:05:46,117 --> 00:05:48,850
What flavor does it taste like?

112
00:05:48,873 --> 00:05:51,407
Mmm, it's sweet.

113
00:05:51,430 --> 00:05:54,900
But it tastes just like strawberry.

114
00:05:54,923 --> 00:05:57,292
Wait, really?

115
00:05:57,315 --> 00:06:01,370
Here, try my Blue Hawaii.

116
00:06:01,394 --> 00:06:04,692
Oh! It tastes the same!

117
00:06:04,716 --> 00:06:10,925
Fun fact: all shaved ice syrups actually taste the same.

118
00:06:10,948 --> 00:06:13,589
No way, is that true?

119
00:06:13,613 --> 00:06:16,046
Unbelievable!

120
00:06:16,069 --> 00:06:19,754
They just have different colors and scents.

121
00:06:19,778 --> 00:06:22,456
That’s mind-blowing!

122
00:06:22,479 --> 00:06:24,517
I had no idea.

123
00:06:24,540 --> 00:06:29,507
But the blue color is so summery and nice.

124
00:06:29,530 --> 00:06:31,343
Yeah, it really is.

125
00:06:31,366 --> 00:06:34,600
It really puts me in a festival mood!

126
00:06:34,623 --> 00:06:37,656
Hey, isn’t your tongue turning blue?

127
00:06:37,679 --> 00:06:40,325
Wait, really?

128
00:06:40,349 --> 00:06:42,949
I don’t have a mirror.

129
00:06:42,972 --> 00:06:46,372
Yep, it’s super blue!

130
00:06:46,395 --> 00:06:48,694
That’s hilarious!

131
00:06:48,717 --> 00:06:52,493
A little embarrassing, but so fun.

132
00:06:52,516 --> 00:06:55,954
This is going to be such a great summer memory.

133
00:06:55,977 --> 00:07:00,247
Yeah, I’m glad we tried the shaved ice!

134
00:07:00,271 --> 00:07:01,771
Scene 4: Unagi and the Day of the Ox – A Midsummer Tradition

135
00:07:01,771 --> 00:07:07,269
Look at all the people lined up in front of that shop!

136
00:07:07,292 --> 00:07:09,067
For sure!

137
00:07:09,090 --> 00:07:11,325
What kind of shop is it?

138
00:07:11,349 --> 00:07:14,085
It’s an unagi (eel) restaurant.

139
00:07:14,108 --> 00:07:16,186
Unagi, huh?

140
00:07:16,210 --> 00:07:19,067
That’s a fancy fish.

141
00:07:19,090 --> 00:07:22,986
Today’s the Day of the Ox, after all.

142
00:07:23,010 --> 00:07:26,050
The Day of the Ox?

143
00:07:26,073 --> 00:07:27,968
What’s that?

144
00:07:27,991 --> 00:07:31,058
It’s a special day in summer.

145
00:07:31,081 --> 00:07:34,014
Everyone eats unagi on this day.

146
00:07:34,037 --> 00:07:37,892
Why do people eat unagi in the summer?

147
00:07:37,916 --> 00:07:42,449
Because unagi gives you energy.

148
00:07:42,472 --> 00:07:45,406
To help you beat the summer heat, right?

149
00:07:45,430 --> 00:07:48,004
Exactly!

150
00:07:48,028 --> 00:07:50,828
It’s an old Japanese tradition.

151
00:07:50,851 --> 00:07:53,184
That’s hilarious!

152
00:07:53,207 --> 00:07:56,007
Let’s get in line too!

153
00:07:56,030 --> 00:07:58,528
There’s a menu over there.

154
00:07:58,552 --> 00:08:00,186
Take a look!

155
00:08:00,209 --> 00:08:04,575
It says 'Pine,' 'Bamboo,' and 'Plum.'

156
00:08:04,598 --> 00:08:06,435
What do those mean?

157
00:08:06,458 --> 00:08:08,992
It's about the grades.

158
00:08:09,015 --> 00:08:12,026
Pine is the highest grade.

159
00:08:12,049 --> 00:08:15,683
The prices are totally different, aren't they?

160
00:08:15,706 --> 00:08:17,985
What's the difference?

161
00:08:18,008 --> 00:08:21,842
The amount and size of the eel vary.

162
00:08:21,865 --> 00:08:25,718
I'll go with the cheapest, Ume.

163
00:08:25,741 --> 00:08:29,741
I'm splurging on Pine.

164
00:08:29,764 --> 00:08:31,297
Huh?

165
00:08:31,320 --> 00:08:33,218
Pine?

166
00:08:33,241 --> 00:08:35,574
Wow, that's impressive.

167
00:08:35,597 --> 00:08:40,431
I waited in line for an hour, so I want to eat a lot.

168
00:08:40,454 --> 00:08:44,022
Oh, we're being shown to our seats.

169
00:08:44,045 --> 00:08:47,112
Mmm, it smells so good.

170
00:08:47,135 --> 00:08:49,535
Here comes the eel.

171
00:08:49,558 --> 00:08:52,691
It looks absolutely delicious.

172
00:08:52,714 --> 00:08:55,647
It's so tender and tasty.

173
00:08:55,670 --> 00:08:57,880
It really gives you energy.

174
00:08:57,903 --> 00:09:01,737
Even Ume is plenty big and delicious.

175
00:09:01,760 --> 00:09:04,993
The sauce is amazing, isn't it?

176
00:09:05,016 --> 00:09:07,694
It makes the rice go down so well.

177
00:09:07,718 --> 00:09:11,119
With this, we'll be fine for the summer.

178
00:09:11,143 --> 00:09:12,720
Sure!

179
00:09:12,743 --> 00:09:16,318
Let's get back to work tomorrow feeling refreshed.

180
00:09:16,342 --> 00:09:18,709
That was delicious.

181
00:09:18,732 --> 00:09:21,532
I want to come back again next year.

182
00:09:21,555 --> 00:09:23,055
Scene 5: The Joys of Izakaya

183
00:09:23,055 --> 00:09:27,055
Japanese izakayas are so much fun.

184
00:09:27,078 --> 00:09:32,678
Yeah, there are so many menu options, it's hard to choose.

185
00:09:32,701 --> 00:09:37,668
Let's start with drinks and edamame.

186
00:09:37,691 --> 00:09:40,024
Edamame?

187
00:09:40,047 --> 00:09:43,580
Those green vegetables, right?

188
00:09:43,603 --> 00:09:48,642
Yes, they come out quickly, so they're great.

189
00:09:48,665 --> 00:09:51,432
Oh, here they are.

190
00:09:51,455 --> 00:09:54,388
That was fast.

191
00:09:54,411 --> 00:09:57,811
They go perfectly with cold beer.

192
00:09:57,834 --> 00:10:00,634
That looks delicious!

193
00:10:00,657 --> 00:10:03,730
Cheers!

194
00:10:03,754 --> 00:10:06,287
Oh, wait a minute.

195
00:10:06,310 --> 00:10:09,409
Don't eat them with the pods.

196
00:10:09,432 --> 00:10:10,704
Huh?

197
00:10:10,727 --> 00:10:13,861
You can't eat the pods?

198
00:10:13,884 --> 00:10:19,350
No, the pods are too tough to eat.

199
00:10:19,373 --> 00:10:21,753
I had no idea.

200
00:10:21,776 --> 00:10:24,435
That was close.

201
00:10:24,459 --> 00:10:29,494
Press the pod with your fingers and eat only the beans inside.

202
00:10:29,517 --> 00:10:31,372
Like this?

203
00:10:31,395 --> 00:10:34,595
Oh, the beans popped out.

204
00:10:34,618 --> 00:10:37,185
That's right.

205
00:10:37,208 --> 00:10:39,008
You're so good at this!

206
00:10:39,031 --> 00:10:42,768
Mmm, this is really good.

207
00:10:42,792 --> 00:10:46,289
The saltiness is just perfect, isn't it?

208
00:10:46,313 --> 00:10:47,999
Sure!

209
00:10:48,022 --> 00:10:51,680
This makes the beer go down so smoothly.

210
00:10:51,703 --> 00:10:54,705
I can't stop eating them.

211
00:10:54,729 --> 00:10:57,107
For sure!

212
00:10:57,130 --> 00:11:00,863
I've already finished them all.

213
00:11:00,886 --> 00:11:03,944
Shall we ask for seconds?

214
00:11:03,968 --> 00:11:06,534
Yes, please.

215
00:11:06,557 --> 00:11:10,624
Next, I'll peel it neatly for us.

216
00:11:10,647 --> 00:11:15,981
If it's delicious and healthy, we can eat a lot, right?

217
00:11:16,005 --> 00:11:19,805
This isn't a food you see much in my country.

218
00:11:19,828 --> 00:11:23,161
It seems like it could get popular overseas too.

219
00:11:23,184 --> 00:11:24,857
Yeah, it really is.

220
00:11:24,881 --> 00:11:28,288
This is one of Japan's must-try cultural experiences.

221
00:11:28,311 --> 00:11:31,386
I want to tell my friends about this.

222
00:11:31,410 --> 00:11:34,543
Don't eat the skin, okay?

223
00:11:34,566 --> 00:11:38,333
That's an important tip.

224
00:11:38,356 --> 00:11:41,689
What should we order next?

225
00:11:41,712 --> 00:11:44,196
Let's get some yakitori.

226
00:11:44,220 --> 00:11:46,553
Sounds good!

227
00:11:46,576 --> 00:11:50,057
A night at an izakaya is the best.

228
00:11:50,080 --> 00:11:51,580
Scene 6: Choosing a Watermelon – A Conversation

229
00:11:51,580 --> 00:11:54,114
Let's go to the supermarket.

230
00:11:54,137 --> 00:11:55,870
Sounds good!

231
00:11:55,893 --> 00:11:59,060
I want to buy some fruit.

232
00:11:59,083 --> 00:12:02,849
Oh, there are watermelons over there!

233
00:12:02,872 --> 00:12:07,306
Wow, that's a huge watermelon!

234
00:12:07,329 --> 00:12:10,495
They're selling whole ones.

235
00:12:10,518 --> 00:12:12,785
Check out the price.

236
00:12:12,809 --> 00:12:15,049
That's too expensive.

237
00:12:15,073 --> 00:12:18,606
In my country, they're much cheaper.

238
00:12:18,629 --> 00:12:22,473
Watermelons in Japan are a bit pricey.

239
00:12:22,496 --> 00:12:26,363
It's too big to fit in the fridge.

240
00:12:26,386 --> 00:12:28,405
Yeah, it really is.

241
00:12:28,429 --> 00:12:32,596
So, let's buy a smaller one.

242
00:12:32,619 --> 00:12:36,652
Oh, here are pre-cut watermelons.

243
00:12:36,675 --> 00:12:41,010
These are cheaper and will fit in the fridge.

244
00:12:41,033 --> 00:12:44,067
Alright, let's get this one.

245
00:12:44,090 --> 00:12:46,493
Let's go home and eat it.

246
00:12:46,516 --> 00:12:49,949
Okay, I've prepared the watermelon.

247
00:12:49,972 --> 00:12:51,839
Here you go.

248
00:12:51,862 --> 00:12:53,742
Thank you.

249
00:12:53,765 --> 00:12:56,011
That looks delicious!

250
00:12:56,035 --> 00:12:59,905
Sprinkle this on it before eating.

251
00:12:59,928 --> 00:13:02,095
What is this?

252
00:13:02,118 --> 00:13:05,185
It's salt.

253
00:13:05,209 --> 00:13:07,825
We put salt on watermelon.

254
00:13:07,848 --> 00:13:09,082
Huh?

255
00:13:09,106 --> 00:13:12,883
You put salt on watermelon?

256
00:13:12,906 --> 00:13:16,597
But watermelon is sweet, right?

257
00:13:16,620 --> 00:13:19,587
Why would you put salt on it?

258
00:13:19,610 --> 00:13:24,108
Because salt makes it taste even sweeter.

259
00:13:24,131 --> 00:13:26,064
Really?

260
00:13:26,087 --> 00:13:28,287
Unbelievable!

261
00:13:28,310 --> 00:13:32,244
Just trust me and try it.

262
00:13:32,267 --> 00:13:34,200
Got it!

263
00:13:34,223 --> 00:13:37,068
I'll just sprinkle a little.

264
00:13:37,092 --> 00:13:39,063
How does it taste?

265
00:13:39,086 --> 00:13:42,623
Oh, wow, it's true!

266
00:13:42,646 --> 00:13:45,653
It's so much sweeter!

267
00:13:45,677 --> 00:13:49,210
It's strange, but it's delicious.

268
00:13:49,233 --> 00:13:52,000
I'm glad you like it.

269
00:13:52,023 --> 00:13:54,556
Eat as much as you want.

270
00:13:54,579 --> 00:13:56,312
Okay!

271
00:13:56,335 --> 00:14:00,902
Japanese culture is truly fascinating, isn't it?

272
00:14:00,925 --> 00:14:02,425
Scene 7: Retro Sightseeing & The Art of Drinking Ramune

273
00:14:02,425 --> 00:14:07,239
Today, we're exploring a retro sightseeing spot.

274
00:14:07,263 --> 00:14:10,130
There's an old-fashioned candy shop here.

275
00:14:10,153 --> 00:14:11,953
Let's go in.

276
00:14:11,976 --> 00:14:15,670
Oh, they sell cold Ramune!

277
00:14:15,693 --> 00:14:17,826
Ramune?

278
00:14:17,849 --> 00:14:21,226
What a beautiful glass bottle!

279
00:14:21,250 --> 00:14:22,984
Let's buy one.

280
00:14:23,007 --> 00:14:25,092
Here you go.

281
00:14:25,116 --> 00:14:26,849
Thank you.

282
00:14:26,872 --> 00:14:30,719
So, how do you drink this?

283
00:14:30,742 --> 00:14:33,709
There's no cap, is there?

284
00:14:33,732 --> 00:14:37,732
Press the plastic stopper down.

285
00:14:37,755 --> 00:14:39,688
This one?

286
00:14:39,711 --> 00:14:44,121
Oh! The marble went inside.

287
00:14:44,145 --> 00:14:45,982
That's right.

288
00:14:46,005 --> 00:14:50,491
Once the marble is in, you can drink it.

289
00:14:50,515 --> 00:14:53,248
What an interesting mechanism!

290
00:14:53,271 --> 00:14:56,604
Cheers!

291
00:14:56,627 --> 00:15:00,227
Huh? The soda won't come out.

292
00:15:00,250 --> 00:15:03,926
Did you tilt the bottle a lot?

293
00:15:03,950 --> 00:15:07,483
Yeah, I tilted it a bunch.

294
00:15:07,506 --> 00:15:09,959
But it still won't come out.

295
00:15:09,983 --> 00:15:15,881
Ah, the marble is stuck in the opening.

296
00:15:15,904 --> 00:15:19,870
You're right, it *is* stuck.

297
00:15:19,893 --> 00:15:22,227
What should we do?

298
00:15:22,250 --> 00:15:27,666
There's a small indentation near the bottle's opening.

299
00:15:27,689 --> 00:15:30,456
An indentation?

300
00:15:30,479 --> 00:15:33,045
Oh, this part here?

301
00:15:33,068 --> 00:15:36,526
Hook the marble onto that spot.

302
00:15:36,550 --> 00:15:38,283
I see.

303
00:15:38,306 --> 00:15:41,515
Let me stop the marble there.

304
00:15:41,539 --> 00:15:45,139
That way, the marble won't fall back in.

305
00:15:45,162 --> 00:15:47,815
Let me try.

306
00:15:47,838 --> 00:15:50,604
Oh! It's coming out now!

307
00:15:50,627 --> 00:15:52,903
Did you get a sip?

308
00:15:52,927 --> 00:15:55,261
Great!

309
00:15:55,284 --> 00:16:00,140
Yes, it's a really delicious soda!

310
00:16:00,163 --> 00:16:05,097
But it's a little tricky to drink.

311
00:16:05,121 --> 00:16:07,773
You need to get the hang of it.

312
00:16:07,796 --> 00:16:10,964
It gets easier with practice.

313
00:16:10,988 --> 00:16:15,521
I love the sound of the marble rattling around!

314
00:16:15,544 --> 00:16:18,559
It sounds like summer, doesn't it?

315
00:16:18,583 --> 00:16:23,616
Yes, it really feels like a Japanese summer.

316
00:16:23,639 --> 00:16:26,093
Should we buy another one?

317
00:16:26,117 --> 00:16:28,127
Sounds good!

318
00:16:28,151 --> 00:16:31,951
I think I can drink it properly next time!

319
00:16:31,974 --> 00:16:33,474
Scene 8: Kawadoko Dining – Savoring Summer Hamo by the River

320
00:16:33,474 --> 00:16:37,725
Summers in Kyoto are so hot, aren't they?

321
00:16:37,748 --> 00:16:39,882
Yeah, it really is.

322
00:16:39,905 --> 00:16:43,842
But it's nice and cool here.

323
00:16:43,865 --> 00:16:48,799
Yeah, the restaurant is right over the river!

324
00:16:48,822 --> 00:16:52,756
This is called *kawadoko*.

325
00:16:52,779 --> 00:16:57,272
You can see the river water—it's so pretty.

326
00:16:57,296 --> 00:17:00,496
The breeze feels amazing, doesn't it?

327
00:17:00,518 --> 00:17:04,328
Here comes the dish!

328
00:17:04,352 --> 00:17:07,685
What a beautiful white fish!

329
00:17:07,708 --> 00:17:10,042
What kind of fish is this?

330
00:17:10,065 --> 00:17:14,031
This is called *hamo*.

331
00:17:14,054 --> 00:17:17,621
It's a high-end summer delicacy.

332
00:17:17,644 --> 00:17:19,244
*Hamo*?

333
00:17:19,267 --> 00:17:22,000
I’ve never heard of it before.

334
00:17:22,023 --> 00:17:26,657
It’s been blanched—quickly dipped in hot water.

335
00:17:26,680 --> 00:17:30,046
Try it with the plum sauce.

336
00:17:30,069 --> 00:17:32,313
That looks delicious!

337
00:17:32,337 --> 00:17:34,138
Bon appétit!

338
00:17:34,162 --> 00:17:39,295
Wait, doesn’t this fish have bones?

339
00:17:39,318 --> 00:17:43,751
Actually, it has *a lot* of bones.

340
00:17:43,774 --> 00:17:48,647
It has *a lot* of bones?!

341
00:17:48,671 --> 00:17:50,071
Sure!

342
00:17:50,094 --> 00:17:53,694
But don’t worry.

343
00:17:53,717 --> 00:17:59,484
The chef has carefully sliced the bones with a knife.

344
00:17:59,507 --> 00:18:02,313
They *cut* the bones?

345
00:18:02,336 --> 00:18:03,993
Sure!

346
00:18:04,016 --> 00:18:08,550
It’s a special technique called *hone-kiri*.

347
00:18:08,573 --> 00:18:13,706
That’s why you can eat it whole, bones and all.

348
00:18:13,729 --> 00:18:16,496
That’s incredible craftsmanship!

349
00:18:16,518 --> 00:18:19,165
Alright, let’s dig in.

350
00:18:19,189 --> 00:18:23,859
Wow, it’s so tender!

351
00:18:23,883 --> 00:18:27,250
I don’t even notice the bones.

352
00:18:27,273 --> 00:18:29,113
Great!

353
00:18:29,136 --> 00:18:32,469
The plum sauce pairs perfectly with it.

354
00:18:32,492 --> 00:18:34,026
Sure!

355
00:18:34,048 --> 00:18:38,382
It’s light, refreshing, and absolutely delicious.

356
00:18:38,405 --> 00:18:41,571
This fish is *made* for summer.

357
00:18:41,594 --> 00:18:46,330
I’ve learned so much about Kyoto’s amazing culture today.

358
00:18:46,354 --> 00:18:51,187
The view is stunning, and the food is incredible.

359
00:18:51,210 --> 00:18:54,879
Thank you so much for bringing me here.

360
00:18:54,902 --> 00:19:00,469
Oh, we’re just getting started—there’s more delicious food to come!

361
00:19:00,492 --> 00:19:02,459
I can’t wait!

362
00:19:02,482 --> 00:19:05,316
Let’s take our time and enjoy.

363
00:19:05,339 --> 00:19:06,839
Scene 9: An Unexpected Encounter at a Café

364
00:19:06,839 --> 00:19:11,639
We’ve been walking a lot in this heat, huh?

365
00:19:11,662 --> 00:19:15,906
Yeah, I’m *so* thirsty.

366
00:19:15,930 --> 00:19:19,063
Let’s duck into this diner.

367
00:19:19,086 --> 00:19:21,102
Sounds good!

368
00:19:21,126 --> 00:19:23,340
Ah, it’s nice and cool in here.

369
00:19:23,363 --> 00:19:26,763
Oh, here comes the tea!

370
00:19:26,786 --> 00:19:31,052
Whoa, that’s a cold drink!

371
00:19:31,075 --> 00:19:34,209
It’s this brown color.

372
00:19:34,232 --> 00:19:39,466
Lucky us—they gave us free iced coffee!

373
00:19:39,489 --> 00:19:43,059
Wait, *iced coffee*?

374
00:19:43,083 --> 00:19:49,416
Yeah, where I’m from, this color means coffee.

375
00:19:49,439 --> 00:19:51,773
Cheers! *glug glug*

376
00:19:51,796 --> 00:19:55,196
*Glug glug.*

377
00:19:55,219 --> 00:19:56,425
Huh?

378
00:19:56,449 --> 00:19:59,908
This tastes *nothing* like coffee.

379
00:19:59,931 --> 00:20:02,131
Isn’t it bitter?

380
00:20:02,154 --> 00:20:04,355
Isn’t it sweet?

381
00:20:04,378 --> 00:20:09,391
Nope, it’s neither bitter *nor* sweet.

382
00:20:09,415 --> 00:20:12,262
Because this *isn’t* coffee.

383
00:20:12,285 --> 00:20:15,918
This is *mugicha*—barley tea.

384
00:20:15,941 --> 00:20:20,708
In Japan, diners often serve this in the summer.

385
00:20:20,731 --> 00:20:23,664
You can drink it for free.

386
00:20:23,687 --> 00:20:27,257
Free is always great, isn't it?

387
00:20:27,281 --> 00:20:29,287
Is this barley tea?

388
00:20:29,310 --> 00:20:32,110
I’ve never tried it before.

389
00:20:32,133 --> 00:20:35,975
It’s so refreshing and really quenches your thirst.

390
00:20:35,998 --> 00:20:40,198
It’s caffeine-free, so it’s good for you.

391
00:20:40,221 --> 00:20:42,622
Oh, I see.

392
00:20:42,645 --> 00:20:45,979
It’s really easy to drink.

393
00:20:46,002 --> 00:20:51,301
I was craving iced coffee, but this is great too.

394
00:20:51,324 --> 00:20:53,757
Do you like it?

395
00:20:53,780 --> 00:20:55,747
I do!

396
00:20:55,770 --> 00:21:00,570
It’s packed with ice and super cold.

397
00:21:00,593 --> 00:21:04,593
Excuse me, may I have a refill?

398
00:21:04,616 --> 00:21:07,470
Drink as much as you like!

399
00:21:07,493 --> 00:21:08,826
Sure!

400
00:21:08,849 --> 00:21:13,493
Barley tea is a must for Japanese summers.

401
00:21:13,516 --> 00:21:16,749
Alright, let’s order some food.

402
00:21:16,772 --> 00:21:19,106
What would you like to eat?

403
00:21:19,129 --> 00:21:22,411
I’d love some chilled udon noodles.

404
00:21:22,434 --> 00:21:23,934
Scene 10: Scorching Heat vs. Fiery Curry – A Summer Showdown

405
00:21:23,934 --> 00:21:29,074
It’s absolutely scorching today, isn’t it?

406
00:21:29,097 --> 00:21:33,830
The sun is so intense—I feel like I’m melting!

407
00:21:33,853 --> 00:21:37,747
On days like this, there’s only one place to go.

408
00:21:37,771 --> 00:21:40,138
A curry shop?

409
00:21:40,161 --> 00:21:43,197
Mmm, it smells amazing in here.

410
00:21:43,221 --> 00:21:48,089
Yes! Their spicy curry is legendary.

411
00:21:48,112 --> 00:21:51,245
Wait—*spicy* curry?

412
00:21:51,268 --> 00:21:54,035
Whoa, that curry is *bright* red!

413
00:21:54,058 --> 00:21:57,946
Oh yeah, it’s *insanely* spicy.

414
00:21:57,970 --> 00:22:00,349
Wait for it...

415
00:22:00,373 --> 00:22:04,307
But it’s already so hot out!

416
00:22:04,330 --> 00:22:08,530
Why would anyone eat something hot *and* spicy in this weather?

417
00:22:08,553 --> 00:22:11,529
Won’t that just make it *hotter*?

418
00:22:11,552 --> 00:22:16,430
Eating spicy food makes you sweat a lot.

419
00:22:16,454 --> 00:22:22,221
And when you sweat, your body cools down afterward.

420
00:22:22,244 --> 00:22:27,584
In Japan, lots of people eat spicy food in the summer.

421
00:22:27,607 --> 00:22:30,376
It really gives you energy!

422
00:22:30,399 --> 00:22:32,566
Seriously?

423
00:22:32,589 --> 00:22:35,122
That sounds too good to be true.

424
00:22:35,145 --> 00:22:37,745
But… okay, I’ll give it a shot.

425
00:22:37,768 --> 00:22:39,972
Let’s do this!

426
00:22:39,996 --> 00:22:42,573
Here comes the curry!

427
00:22:42,596 --> 00:22:44,396
Here you go.

428
00:22:44,419 --> 00:22:49,352
Whoa—the *smell* alone is making me sweat!

429
00:22:49,375 --> 00:22:51,508
Bon appétit!

430
00:22:51,531 --> 00:22:55,098
H-holy cow, this is *spicy*!

431
00:22:55,121 --> 00:22:57,354
Here, have some water.

432
00:22:57,377 --> 00:22:59,990
A-are you okay?

433
00:23:00,014 --> 00:23:03,814
Even the water burns!

434
00:23:03,837 --> 00:23:06,837
My mouth is on fire!

435
00:23:06,860 --> 00:23:10,661
But… I can’t stop eating it!

436
00:23:10,684 --> 00:23:12,451
Sure!

437
00:23:12,474 --> 00:23:15,074
It’s *so* spicy…

438
00:23:15,097 --> 00:23:19,064
But it’s *so* good!

439
00:23:19,087 --> 00:23:22,253
That’s the umami kicking in!

440
00:23:22,276 --> 00:23:25,876
Sweat is dripping down my forehead.

441
00:23:25,899 --> 00:23:28,466
Feels so refreshing, doesn't it?

442
00:23:28,489 --> 00:23:30,226
Absolutely!

443
00:23:30,250 --> 00:23:34,135
Strangely, I'm starting to feel refreshed.

444
00:23:34,159 --> 00:23:39,434
See? It feels cooler once you step outside the shop.

445
00:23:39,457 --> 00:23:41,702
For sure!

446
00:23:41,726 --> 00:23:45,328
Doesn't it feel less hot than before?

447
00:23:45,351 --> 00:23:49,370
Summer's fiery hot curry—it's the best, right?

448
00:23:49,394 --> 00:23:51,401
Sure!

449
00:23:51,424 --> 00:23:54,791
I think I'm getting hooked.

450
00:23:54,814 --> 00:23:57,092
Let's come again.